// --- The ravine: lava down below, a ledge on the far side, and a ridge ---
//
// The lava runs round the south end of the castle as well. It does not flow:
// the parapet hides it from the walk, and flowing lava is cut on a fine grid
// that, over an area this size, cost more to draw than the rest of the view.
// The ridge is two rows of rock, the nearer one lower, so its top edge is
// broken against the sky behind it rather than standing up as one wall. The
// rock all round is cut into strips of random width, each with a tilted top
// and faces that lean back from the lava, more steeply above a crease. The
// cliff under the castle keeps its top edge and splays out into the lava.
{
"classname" "func_group"
